WEBVTT

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.030
This is the Mongoose Squadron.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.380
We've reached the designated point.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.470
This is Wilbor-1.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.690
I don't see anything.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:30.710
It's all rocks.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.060
C-2, roger.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.770
Move our area of operations towards the target.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:36.980
Don't let your guard down.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.060
Roger that.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:44.780
What's wrong?

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.660
It's a person!

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.990
There's a person standing there!

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.910
A-A woman?!

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.770
What is it?!

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.100
What happened, Wilbor?

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.990
Damn it! The heli's down!

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.890
I repeat! The heli's down!

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.080
C-2, what happened?!

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.330
Did you get attacked?!

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.330
Fall back!

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.370
Retreat!

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.440
Retreat at once!

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:30.860
Damn it!

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.470
Wiped out?!

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.270
That's impossible!

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:52.750
What's wrong?!

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.980
Yoryoko's sunk!

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:59.380
A sonic wave just...

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.310
What?!

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.960
T-This is...

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.950
Magnificent.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.910
I just thought of something marvelous.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:22.400
A thunderclap...

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.710
Like the gods...

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:30.800
We shall bring forth a miraculous legend using our hands.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:50.360
atarashii yakusoku ga kokoro wo tsuyoku tsunagu

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:50.360
Our new promise binds our hearts together strongly

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:57.450
kawaru sekai ni kane ga hibiku yukou

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:57.450
The bell rings in the changing world, let's go

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:04.290
owari naki tatakai ga subete wo hiki saitemo

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:04.290
Even if the endless fight shreds everything apart,

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:10.490
kimi no hohoemi tada shinjite

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:10.490
I will believe in your smile

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:14.680
kimi no yume mamoreru nara

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:14.680
If I can protect your dream,

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.260
itami sae dakishimeyou

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.260
I will even embrace pain

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:27.600
kasane au kono omoi mune no chikai yuzurenai

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:27.600
I can't let go of these piling feelings, this oath in my heart

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:34.340
aa, sora no haruka hate made

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:34.340
Ah, all the way to the end of the sky,

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:42.540
sou, kakete yuku you na kasoku shiteku jounetsu

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:39.130
yes, my passion accelerates

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.540
as if it were rushing through my body

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:48.730
aa, donna unmei datte

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:48.730
Ah, no matter what kind of fate awaits me,

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:59.880
sou, takaku koeteku makenai yuuki kureta kara

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:53.040
yes, I can fly high over it

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:59.880
because you gave me this undefeatable courage

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:10.480
Quiet Omen

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:10.480
First Feather

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:19.560
The barricades between the Capital and other cities are still in effect and under control of MBI.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.290
The flood of terrorist threats still hasn't ceased,

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:27.370
and therefore Minaka Hirotoshi, the President of MBI, has indefinitely extended the ban.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:31.320
Looks like they've gotten even more cautious about it.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.270
In this city of Shin-Touteitou,

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:40.650
there reside 108 beings called Sekirei along with their partners, Ashikabi.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:46.940
They fight each other until there's only one left standing.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.820
That is "The Sekirei Project."

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:55.530
And so, I'm one of those Ashikabi,

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:58.150
and Kuu-chan here is a Sekirei.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:02.170
To think that I actually got caught up in this mess...

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.390
A part of me still can't believe it.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:06.970
Minato-san!

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.290
What's up, Musubi-chan?

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.630
I want to get a pot from the top shelf,

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.260
but I just can't reach it.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:23.560
I'll get it for you.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:25.250
Thank you very much!

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.480
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.150
It's painful, but... I'm a bit happy as well.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.170
So you're making lunch today?

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:43.970
Yes. The Landlady is out so I'm doing it.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.870
Then let me help you.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.130
Thank you very much.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:50.820
So, could you peel the onions?

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:51.580
Sure.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:54.930
My eyes are tearing up.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:56.960
Are you all right?

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.760
As I thought, she is cute...

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:08.680
Musubi-chan here is the first Sekirei I met.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:11.140
Ah, don't move, please.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.370
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.570
It's unfair that it's only Mu-chan!

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.570
I'm going to help too!

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.890
But... We're using knives and fire, so it's dangerous.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:23.130
Just leave this to me!

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:25.910
Kuu-chan?

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.960
We'll let you help next time, so...

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:35.370
Kuu's going to help too!

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.600
The vegetables are growing!

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.850
Kuu-chan!

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:42.600
Don't!

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.720
Don't make the vegetables grow!

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:47.600
Matsu-san!

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.600
It's definitely an explosion of Kusano-tan's power of jealousy.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.280
H-How did you get up there?

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.500
Don't just laugh there, do something!

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.000
This person, Matsu-san, is also my Sekirei.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:04.980
Even if you say that...

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:11.250
I can't move.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:13.960
What do you call this again?

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.800
"The wives' bondage play in the afternoon's kitchen."

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:21.170
Don't give it such a lewd title!

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:23.800
Kuu-chan! Where are you?!

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:27.560
All of you! What the hell are you doing while it's still bright outside...?

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:28.720
Tsukiumi?!

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:29.730
Minato!

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:35.140
Leaving your real wife behind...
a-and performing such lewd playful acts!

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:38.880
S-So to you, it looks like we're playing...

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.910
Obviously, Tsukiumi is also one of mine.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.490
Water Celebration!

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:49.000
Tsukiumi-tan! Don't use water!

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.450
It'll make the plants grow even more!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.040
Huh?

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.530
I see.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:07:59.670
So that's why...

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.670
I'm sorry, Landlady.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:04.480
The lunch isn't ready yet.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.060
Musubi-chan! That isn't what you should be apologizing for!

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:12.810
Those kinds of impure and degrading plays are forbidden at Izumo Inn.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:18.610
Does it look like we're playing around to you, too?

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:26.570
I'm definitely going to die if I get any more Sekirei than this.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:33.020
I thought it was loud. I can't even take a nap.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.580
I will be frank with you, Kazehana.

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:42.350
It's not like I've accepted you as a resident here.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.300
You're so mean, Miya.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:51.570
Oh, right. Today's the day your husband passed away, isn't it?

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:55.940
I wonder what he'd think about the current situation if he were alive.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:57.940
If he...

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:04.280
If he were still alive, he would have never forgiven this kind of situation.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.510
Never.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:15.790
The body of a Sekirei reacts unwillingly once they meet their fated Ashikabi.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:22.570
Whether they consider it a blessing or a misfortune,

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.020
that's up to them.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.880
Well? So what about you, Kazehana?

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:33.430
Dang. So you noticed, huh?

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:38.580
That's the reason why you left this place but returned again, isn't it?

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:43.240
Bonding with an Ashikabi and getting winged is a Sekirei's fate.

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:48.060
I don't think you can just keep watching from the sidelines forever.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.240
A maiden's heart is complicated.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:59.370
The reason why I'm here is to see if that man can make me feel that way.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.590
Here, Kuu-chan.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:12.620
I-I've always been wondering about this, but...
how do Sekirei fit all this in their stomachs?

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.520
Oh, Uzume-san!

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:19.680
It's curry for lunch, huh?

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.100
Uzume-san, good morning!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.510
Morning.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.860
Isn't it pretty late for lunch though?

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.110
Well, some things happened.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.500
Some things happened.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:31.610
S-Some things happened.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.430
Huh?

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.180
Well, that's too bad.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:39.500
I love your curry, too.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.720
You're not going to eat?

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:43.890
I've got some stuff to take care of.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:46.540
Then, we'll leave some for you!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:47.500
Really?

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:51.510
Kusano is such a good girl.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.410
Well then, I'll be going.

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:55.680
Have a safe trip.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.170
Is something wrong?

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:03.800
It looks like Uzume-san hasn't been feeling all that well lately.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.020
Really?

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.640
I hope it's just my imagination.

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:16.740
What's up, Kagari? Making a scary face like that...

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.950
I want to tell you something.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:26.010
I'm the Sekirei's Guardian, so forgiving the clothed Sekirei would be difficult for me.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:35.470
However, Uzume is our friend who lives here with us.

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:38.040
Should something ever happen, you can come to me any time.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:40.830
Jeez, Kagari. What are you talking about?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.360
There's nothing going on.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:44.120
But,

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.930
if I suddenly dissappear,

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:52.080
just think that Uzume isn't here anymore.

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:54.280
What do you mean by that?

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:56.780
Later.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:07.380
I guess we can only look over her for now.

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.890
Matsu-san, the lunch is ready!

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.840
O-Okay!

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:14.420
What's wrong?

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.230
No, it's nothing at all.

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:23.280
Matsu-san?!

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.280
Since we're already at it...

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:26.770
At what?!

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:29.600
If you mention a Sekirei and Ashikabi's long awaited moment...

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.900
W-Wait a second!

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:39.650
Deepening the relationship between Sekirei and Ashikabi is also a factor of winning in The Sekirei Project.

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:42.500
A road that cannot be taken by a strategist...

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:46.210
Prepare yourself, Mina-tan...

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.980
No lunch for you two.

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:56.290
Me too?!

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:05.420
It got this late already.

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:09.490
It's been a while.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:10.320
What is it?

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.640
No. 95.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.120
It's about Kuno.

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:20.020
You helped No. 95 escape from the Capital.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:25.040
T-That's...

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:27.830
Higa-sama should have specifically told you to defeat her.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:34.860
Even if I didn't defeat her, I thought that running away from the Capital was the same as retiring from The Sekirei Project.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:38.880
That's not for you to decide.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.510
I wonder how long your Ashikabi's life is going to last.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:45.470
Next time, I'll definitely... So leave Chiho out of it.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.430
There'll be a new order soon enough.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.380
Keep that in mind, please.

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:51.770
I got it.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:56.370
Come in.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:58.800
Chiho, sorry!

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:00.860
Uzume-chan!

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:02.870
I overslept.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:06.540
It's okay. I'm just happy that you came.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:07.940
How are you feeling?

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:09.830
Is it painful at all?

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.210
I'm fine.

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:15.000
You ask the same thing every time you're here.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.170
Is that so?

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.010
What's wrong, Uzume-chan?

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:25.150
I was just thinking about how glad I am to know that you're my Ashikabi.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:29.470
But, I can't do anything for you.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:34.570
None of that matters. Because I love you.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.930
Thank you, Uzume-chan.

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:40.490
The sky's so blue today.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:46.340
I hope I can see the sky from outside of this window one day.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.060
You will.

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:49.020
Definitely.

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:58.370
I looked through the MBI's Disciplinary Squad's database.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:14:59.830
Database?

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:05.230
You were curious about it and you told me to look into it.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.980
Oh, that?

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:09.190
You're curious too, aren't you?

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:10.730
That time...

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.070
Disciplinary Squad Leader,

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:14.590
The Sekirei of Fate,

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:16.490
No. 08 Yume.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.880
Her name was definitely there.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.530
The second generation leader,

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:22.440
No. 08 Yume.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.650
Second generation?

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.920
Does that mean Karasuba's the third then?

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:31.400
The Disciplinary Squad is in its third generation.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:35.460
The second generation were No. 08 and Karasuba.

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:37.590
But that's all I found out.

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:39.490
Huh? What is that suppose to mean?

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:41.030
Who's the first?

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:44.480
There were traces of data being erased.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:45.880
I don't get it!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.220
It pisses me off.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:48.840
So what does that mean then?

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.250
Is No. 88 Musubi also No. 08?

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:53.440
That's incorrect.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:56.950
Karasuba.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:01.500
Yume and Musubi are two separate beings.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.440
Huh? I still don't get it.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.630
It's okay if you don't.

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:08.500
Yume doesn't exist anymore.

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.620
The first retired, too.

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:12.790
What do you mean she doesn't exist anymore?

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.630
You got beaten up pretty badly, didn't you, Benitsubasa?

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.050
If you think you can do it, go ahead.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:20.970
I'll do so even if you don't tell me!

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:24.890
I'm looking forward to it.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:29.110
Pull that person out again.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:41.430
It's so annoying.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:42.440
Huh?

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:44.580
What is it?

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:47.080
We've received news from Intel.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:48.530
A runaway.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:51.600
I'll go.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.510
Can we really get away?

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:02.600
Yeah. MBI's hiding it,

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:06.480
but it looks like there really was an Ashikabi and a Sekirei that got out of the Capital.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:11.040
If we really can get out of this killing game...

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:17.520
You sure said something interesting.

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:18.390
Who are you?!

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:21.810
No. 105, Benitsubasa of the Disciplinary Squad.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:23.860
Disciplinary Squad?

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:25.310
What do we do?

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.690
What do we do, you ask?

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:30.610
We just have to beat her up and get out!

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:46.350
Try beating me up.

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:53.060
You're too weak!

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:58.180
Damn it.

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:00.050
It's so annoying.

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:06.880
How rare.

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:10.570
It looks like you haven't been here in a while.

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:14.240
The moon is so pretty, after all. Drinking alone while watching the moon isn't so bad sometimes.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.200
Then I must be bothering you.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:20.120
If I stay there, my body gets so hot that I feel like I'm about to suffocate.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.460
So, what about you?

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:24.050
W-What are you talking about?

00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:26.470
You're reacting to someone as well, right?

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:31.680
I won't become anyone's possession. Nor do I plan on ever doing so.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.680
Ah, that's too bad.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:35.350
Even though love is so wonderful.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:38.850
The wind has started to change.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:44.310
It looks like there's a storm coming soon.

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:48.060
Sahashi-san, go ahead and take a bath before dinner.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.950
Okay, thank you!

00:18:56.290 --> 00:18:58.810
I really didn't get lunch.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:02.760
It's just one factor of winning in The Sekirei Project.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:07.180
The Sekirei Project, huh?

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:12.000
It sure has been eerily quiet ever since the escape plan.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:16.230
It would be nice if we could just keep on living peacefully like this.

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:20.790
Minato-san?

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.530
It's time for dinner!

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.120
Minato-sa-

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:37.070
Minato-san?

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.650
What is this place?

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:04.740
What's wrong, Minato-san?

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.150
Musubi-chan.

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:09.090
I just had a weird dream.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.080
W-Why are you here?!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:17.850
You were sleeping so peacefully, so I thought it would be rude to wake you up.

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:22.500
Since this was a rare moment, I got in too.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:27.260
"A rare moment"? Aren't you acting like Matsu-san...

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:30.760
Wait. We were in here together this whole time?

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:33.550
This whole time.

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:34.760
Eh?!

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:37.260
If someone sees us in here-

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:45.870
I thought something was off when Musubi didn't come back after going to get you...

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.030
No, this isn't what it looks like!

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:51.030
I was just zoning out!

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.110
No excuses!

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:54.330
Hey- Wait!

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.770
Calm down!

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.060
Water Celebration!

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:02.370
What a massacre.

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:05.110
While they're still at it, I'll join in too.

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:10.770
Minato!

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:12.220
Wait a minute!

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:14.690
Water Celebration!

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:18.810
I just got a good idea.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:26.770
Finally, the curtain to Act 2 has fallen.

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:29.310
I will no longer allow any distractions.

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:33.680
Come, follow your fate and fight.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.750
And write it!

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:38.120
A new legend.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:40.340
A miraculous love story!

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:20.370
Finally, the new season of Sekirei has begun!

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.280
Let's work hard from now on once more, Musubi-chan!

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:25.720
Yes! Musubi will give it her all for Minato-san.

00:23:25.890 --> 00:23:28.620
I'll fight, lose, show things, shake things!

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:30.280
The goal is uncensoring only on limited editions!

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.280
Eh? W-Wait, Musubi-chan?

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:34.060
Second Wing: The Wind Swells

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:38.040
Tune in next week!
